@* LoginPage: the sign-in form at "/login".

   Static server-side rendered on purpose: it is an ordinary HTML form that posts to /auth/login (with an
   antiforgery token), so signing in works without a live connection and the endpoint can set the cookie.
   The return address travels in a hidden field and is checked again by the endpoint. A failed attempt comes
   back here with "error=1"; the message is the same whatever went wrong, so it never reveals whether a user
   name exists. A client that made too many attempts comes back with "error=throttled" and a message that is
   the same for every name; any other non-empty value shows the generic message. After a forced password change the
   account page sends the user here with "changed=1", which shows a notice to sign in with the new password.
   When sign-in with an OpenID Connect provider is enabled, a second card offers a "Sign in with ..." button (a
   form that posts to /auth/oidc/login with its own antiforgery token); "error=oidc" shows one generic message
   next to that button, whatever went wrong at the provider. *@
@page "/login"

<PageTitle>Sign in - ReviewCenter</PageTitle>

<main class="page narrow" data-testid="login-page">
    <h1>Sign in</h1>

    @if (PasswordChanged)
    {
        <p class="notice" role="status" data-testid="login-password-changed">
            Password changed. Sign in with your new password.
        </p>
    }

    <section class="card">
        <form method="post" action="/auth/login" data-testid="login-form">
            <AntiforgeryToken />
            <input type="hidden" name="returnUrl" value="@SafeReturnUrl" />
            <div class="field">
                <label for="login-username">User name</label>
                <input id="login-username" name="username" type="text" autocomplete="username"
                       data-testid="login-username-input" />
            </div>
            <div class="field">
                <label for="login-password">Password</label>
                <input id="login-password" name="password" type="password" autocomplete="current-password"
                       data-testid="login-password-input" />
            </div>
            @if (Throttled)
            {
                <p class="error" role="alert" data-testid="login-throttled">Too many sign-in attempts. Try again in a few minutes.</p>
            }
            else if (Failed && !ProviderFailed)
            {
                <p class="error" role="alert" data-testid="login-error">Invalid user name or password.</p>
            }
            <button type="submit" data-testid="login-button">Sign in</button>
        </form>
    </section>

    @if (Provider.Enabled)
    {
        <section class="card" data-testid="oidc-card">
            <p class="muted" data-testid="oidc-lead">Or use the account you have at @Provider.DisplayName.</p>
            @if (ProviderFailed)
            {
                <p class="error" role="alert" data-testid="oidc-error">
                    Sign-in with @Provider.DisplayName did not work. Try again or ask an administrator.
                </p>
            }
            <form method="post" action="/auth/oidc/login" data-testid="oidc-form">
                <AntiforgeryToken />
                <input type="hidden" name="returnUrl" value="@SafeReturnUrl" />
                <button type="submit" class="secondary" data-testid="oidc-login">Sign in with @Provider.DisplayName</button>
            </form>
        </section>
    }
</main>
